{"name":"Destroying Angels","hex":"#e9e9e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"destroying angels","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of destroying angel"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destroying_angels"}],"entries":[{"title":"Destroying angel (Bible)","blocks":[{"text":"In the Hebrew Bible, the destroying angel, also known as mashḥit, is an entity sent out by God on several occasions to deal with numerous peoples."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/The_destroying_angel_passes_through_Egypt.jpg/330px-The_destroying_angel_passes_through_Egypt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destroying_angel_(Bible)"},{"title":"Danite","blocks":[{"text":"The Danites were a fraternal organization founded by Latter Day Saint members in June 1838, in the town of Far West, Caldwell County, Missouri."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Charge_of_the_Danites.jpg/330px-Charge_of_the_Danites.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danite"},{"title":"Destroying Angels (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Destroying Angels\" is a 2018 stand-alone single released by alternative rock band Garbage with John Doe and Exene Cervenka of the American punk rock band X. The song was written and recorded for 2018's Black Friday Record Store Day event in North America, with a digital release worldwide the following year."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e9/DestroyingAngelsCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destroying_Angels_(song)"},{"title":"Destroying angel","blocks":[{"text":"Destroying angels are several similar, closely related species of deadly all-white mushrooms in the genus Amanita. They are Amanita virosa in Europe and A. bisporigera and A. ocreata in eastern and western North America, respectively. Another European species of Amanita referred to as the destroying angel, Amanita verna—also referred to as the \"fool's mushroom\"—was first described in France in 1780. Destroying angels are among the most toxic known mushrooms; both they and the closely related death caps contain amatoxins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Destroying_Angel.jpg/330px-Destroying_Angel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destroying_angel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Last_Public_Address_of_Lieutenant_General_Joseph_Smith.jpg/500px-Last_Public_Address_of_Lieutenant_General_Joseph_Smith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Last_Public_Address_of_Lieutenant_General_Joseph_Smith.jpg/500px-Last_Public_Address_of_Lieutenant_General_Joseph_Smith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALast_Public_Address_of_Lieutenant_General_Joseph_Smith.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Battle_of_Crooked_River.jpg/500px-Battle_of_Crooked_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Battle_of_Crooked_River.jpg/500px-Battle_of_Crooked_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Click the image for an enlarged map illustrating the Battle of Crooked River.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABattle_of_Crooked_River.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Destroying_Angel_02.jpg/500px-Destroying_Angel_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Destroying_Angel_02.jpg/1280px-Destroying_Angel_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Destroying_Angel_02.jpg/500px-Destroying_Angel_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A growing destroying angel (specifically the species Amanita virosa) in Ludvika, Sweden","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADestroying_Angel_02.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}